window.CARDS=window.CARDS||{};CARDS["world-uninhabited-island"]=[{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ibuki-mio hirata-yousuke kanzaki-ryuuji ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  the camera in the luggage  the morning watch  kanzaki s visit pre dawn heat in the class d tent  ayanokoji slips out while the class sleeps and goes through the piled luggage  the island morning  the mesh tent keeps the night breeze  the luggage is stacked outside to save space  and dawn comes on hot  opens ibuki s singularly colored bag and finds a digital camera with a rental sticker    this item wasn t appropriate for a deserted island  checks the camera s power source    it had no data  and no sign that it d been used    returns it to the bag  and reasons out why she would carry it  the camera explains the dull sound he heard when she dropped the bag against a tree the day before  shares the early watch with hirata while the rest of the class sleeps on   i guess if i had to pick  school life s my priority  besides  i don t think it s possible to reach class a  after everyone is asleep  cuts one of the manual s five blank pages  replicates a simple island map  folds it into a small square and pockets it  reads the heart bedazzled gifts in hirata s pack as karuizawa s  meets kanzaki at the river with hirata and takes in the class b campsite directions  weighs that kanzaki  ichinose and horikita had worked together in the false accusation case   probably why he thinks they are still on good terms  reads the visit as reconnaissance    you could estimate the number of points spent just by the number of toilets  showers  and tents  the second spot update was postponed so ownership expires right after eight o clock  letting the roll call crowds camouflage the renewal","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\">Ch.3: the camera in the luggage, the morning watch, Kanzaki&#x27;s visit<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.100–104<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Pre-dawn heat in the Class D tent; Ayanokōji slips out while the class sleeps and goes through the piled luggage.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../people/kanzaki-ryuuji.html\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I guess if I had to pick, school life&#x27;s my priority. Besides, I don&#x27;t think it&#x27;s possible to reach Class A.”<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>11 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The island morning: the mesh tent keeps the night breeze, the luggage is stacked outside to save space, and dawn comes on hot.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Opens Ibuki&#x27;s singularly colored bag and finds a digital camera with a rental sticker — “This item wasn&#x27;t appropriate for a deserted island.”<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Checks the camera&#x27;s power source — “It had no data, and no sign that it&#x27;d been used.” — returns it to the bag, and reasons out why she would carry it.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> The camera explains the dull sound he heard when she dropped the bag against a tree the day before.<span class=\"pg\">p.100<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Shares the early watch with Hirata while the rest of the class sleeps on.<span class=\"pg\">p.100–101<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> After everyone is asleep, cuts one of the manual&#x27;s five blank pages, replicates a simple island map, folds it into a small square and pockets it.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Reads the heart-bedazzled gifts in Hirata&#x27;s pack as Karuizawa&#x27;s.<span class=\"pg\">p.102<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kanzaki Ryūji<\/b> Meets Kanzaki at the river with Hirata and takes in the Class B campsite directions.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Weighs that Kanzaki, Ichinose and Horikita had worked together in the false accusation case — probably why he thinks they are still on good terms.<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Reads the visit as reconnaissance — “You could estimate the number of points spent just by the number of toilets, showers, and tents.”<span class=\"pg\">p.103<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> The second spot update was postponed so ownership expires right after eight o&#x27;clock, letting the roll-call crowds camouflage the renewal.<span class=\"pg\">p.104<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p87-1\">← Before: Ch.2 §2.8: the points speech, the river vote, and Kouenji&#x27;s exit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action","w":"ike-kanji ibuki-mio horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  3 1  class c comes to provoke morning roll call over  exploration begins  two class c boys stride into the campsite eating chips  the campsite after roll call  the river base holding  class d setting out to explore  recognizes komiya and kondou and recalls their earlier fight with sudo as acting on ryuen s orders rather than just looking for a fight  stands with ike when the chips are tossed at his feet  neither takes the bait until hirata s group returns  files ibuki s worst case remark and decides telling horikita  seemed like a good idea  pulls the leader out of the tent    you ve got eyes on ryuuen  and you ve even been observing ichinose  people will remember that you re the student council president s younger sister  no matter what you do  you ll be a target","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\">Ch.3 §3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.105–107<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Morning roll call over, exploration begins; two Class C boys stride into the campsite eating chips.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../people/ike-kanji.html\">Ike Kanji<\/a> · <a href=\"../people/ibuki-mio.html\">Ibuki Mio<\/a> · <a href=\"../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q action\">Recognizes Komiya and Kondou and recalls their earlier fight with Sudō as acting on Ryūen&#x27;s orders rather than just looking for a fight.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>4 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The campsite after roll call, the river base holding, Class D setting out to explore.<span class=\"pg\">p.105<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ike Kanji<\/b> Stands with Ike when the chips are tossed at his feet; neither takes the bait until Hirata&#x27;s group returns.<span class=\"pg\">p.105–106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ibuki Mio<\/b> Files Ibuki&#x27;s worst-case remark and decides telling Horikita “seemed like a good idea.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Pulls the leader out of the tent — “You&#x27;ve got eyes on Ryuuen, and you&#x27;ve even been observing Ichinose. People will remember that you&#x27;re the student council president&#x27;s younger sister. No matter what you do, you&#x27;ll be a target.”<span class=\"pg\">p.106–107<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p100-1\">← Before: Ch.3: the camera in the luggage, the morning watch, Kanzaki&#x27;s visit<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.2: Ryūen&#x27;s beach, spent to zero<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  3 2  ryuen s beach  spent to zero the class c beach  temporary toilets and showers  a tarp  a barbecue  chairs  a parasol  jet skis on the shoreline  the class c shore  cooking smoke  laughter  a hundred and fifty points or more already burned   it s up to you  horikita  the line names horikita as the one addressed  the translation never tags the speaker  stands through ryuen pouring out his water and throwing the warm bottle back at ishizaki without intervening  leaves with her after the first name call and the crotch grab provocation  stopping once on the way back to look over the class c camp  works out the zero points strategy  nothing left to penalize  and even guesses of every rival leader s identity could gain only  a maximum of 150 points   that s simple  he d just do what kouenji did  the plan at zero points is retirement    his physical condition was poor and he was mentally unstable  in that case  it s better to just retire  the walk back exchange never tags its speakers until horikita s final line  these lines are recorded here as the responses to her questions","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p108-1\">Ch.3 §3.2: Ryūen&#x27;s beach, spent to zero<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.108–115<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The Class C beach: temporary toilets and showers, a tarp, a barbecue, chairs, a parasol, jet skis on the shoreline.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It&#x27;s up to you, Horikita.”<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “That&#x27;s simple. He&#x27;d just do what Kouenji did.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>7 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The Class C shore: cooking smoke, laughter, a hundred and fifty points or more already burned.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line names Horikita as the one addressed; the translation never tags the speaker.<span class=\"pg\">p.108<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Stands through Ryūen pouring out his water and throwing the warm bottle back at Ishizaki without intervening.<span class=\"pg\">p.111–112<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Leaves with her after the first-name call and the crotch-grab provocation, stopping once on the way back to look over the Class C camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.114<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Works out the zero-points strategy: nothing left to penalize, and even guesses of every rival leader&#x27;s identity could gain only “a maximum of 150 points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.113<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> The plan at zero points is retirement — “His physical condition was poor and he was mentally unstable. In that case, it&#x27;s better to just retire.”<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The walk-back exchange never tags its speakers until Horikita&#x27;s final line; these lines are recorded here as the responses to her questions.<span class=\"pg\">p.115<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p105-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.1: Class C comes to provoke<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\">→ After: Ch.3: walking back from the Class C shore<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"ichinose-honami kushida-kikyou horikita-suzune kaneda-satoru ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  3 3  class b s camp at the well deep forest past the broken landmark tree  class b s base is set around a well with hammocks strung between the trees  ichinose tying a cord  kanzaki sitting a little way off  class b s site   trees around a well  hammocks instead of tents  and a path of student tracks already beaten through the forest  reads the broken tree as a landmark the school left on purpose  which is why kanzaki s directions needed no detail   well  i suppose it s just what we d expect from class b   your class seems to be functioning well  despite obstacles   i m sorry if we re getting in the way  the three lines are untagged  ichinose takes up and answers each of them  she reads the visit as a request and welcomes them without any hint of protest   what s a water shower  i m a little curious about that  judges the water shower probably less effective than the temporary shower because it costs five points less  and passes on it   did you already know about them  water showers  i mean  class b s purchases itemize to exactly seventy points once the food is counted  sets that total against class d with koenji s retirement already deducted  weighs the foraging against the fruit kushida s group carried back for class d  watches the class b method in one pass  the well tested before anyone drinks  hot water on a gas can  unlimited vinyl sheets granted with the temporary toilet  and water sprinkled to pull the heat out of the soil  he stays silent while she lays out class d s side and runs the exchange  the visitors  questions about hard ground and the heat are never tagged and are left as a chapter attribution gap  names him as a class c student before ichinose can finish answering   a class c student  files him as the class c boy who resisted ryuen and was taken in by class b   i think it s about time to get going  ayanokouji kun  we ll be a bother to class b if we linger too long  says farewell with horikita and leaves the camp  sets class d against class b on the way out  class d has selfish students like koenji who run off alone  and nobody with the power to step in  the two untagged verdict lines that follow the departure are left as a chapter attribution gap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: Class B’s camp at the well<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.117–125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Deep forest past the broken landmark tree: Class B&#x27;s base is set around a well with hammocks strung between the trees, Ichinose tying a cord, Kanzaki sitting a little way off.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a> · <a href=\"../people/kushida-kikyou.html\">Kushida Kikyō<\/a> · <a href=\"../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../people/kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Well, I suppose it’s just what we’d expect from Class B…”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Your class seems to be functioning well, despite obstacles.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m sorry if we’re getting in the way.”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> Class B&#x27;s site — trees around a well, hammocks instead of tents, and a path of student tracks already beaten through the forest.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the broken tree as a landmark the school left on purpose, which is why Kanzaki&#x27;s directions needed no detail.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The three lines are untagged; Ichinose takes up and answers each of them.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> She reads the visit as a request and welcomes them without any hint of protest.<span class=\"pg\">p.117–118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “What’s a water shower? I’m a little curious about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Judges the water shower probably less effective than the temporary shower because it costs five points less, and passes on it.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you already know about them? Water showers, I mean,”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> Class B&#x27;s purchases itemize to exactly seventy points once the food is counted.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Sets that total against Class D with Kōenji&#x27;s retirement already deducted.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kushida Kikyō<\/b> Weighs the foraging against the fruit Kushida&#x27;s group carried back for Class D.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Watches the Class B method in one pass: the well tested before anyone drinks, hot water on a gas can, unlimited vinyl sheets granted with the temporary toilet, and water sprinkled to pull the heat out of the soil.<span class=\"pg\">p.120–122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> He stays silent while she lays out Class D&#x27;s side and runs the exchange.<span class=\"pg\">p.121–123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The visitors&#x27; questions about hard ground and the heat are never tagged and are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Names him as a Class C student before Ichinose can finish answering.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A Class C student?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Position<\/span> Files him as the Class C boy who resisted Ryūen and was taken in by Class B.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think it’s about time to get going, Ayanokouji-kun. We’ll be a bother to Class B if we linger too long.”<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> Says farewell with Horikita and leaves the camp.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Sets Class D against Class B on the way out: Class D has selfish students like Kōenji who run off alone, and nobody with the power to step in.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The two untagged verdict lines that follow the departure are left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p116-1\">← Before: Ch.3: walking back from the Class C shore<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\">→ After: Ch.3 §3.4: the Class A cave<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p117-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"horikita-suzune hirata-yousuke kaneda-satoru ichinose-honami","q":"ichinose honami ch 3  3 3  the camp that already works class b s base around the well  she is tying a hammock cord to a tree when horikita and ayanokoji walk in  and kanzaki sits a little way off  class b s site   trees around a well  hammocks strung for lack of tent space  unfamiliar equipment beside the water   huh  horikita san  and ayanokouji kun   ha ha  yeah  it was really difficult at first  but we tried a bunch of different things  and it worked out  though the list of chores just keeps on increasing  there s still a ton of work left  takes the interruption as a welcome rather than an intrusion  smiling  she assumes they came with a question   oh  i m sorry  that probably sounded like i was trying to drive you guys away  i think it s all right if you hang around for a while  you probably came here to ask me something  right  welcomes them without any hint of protest and invites them to sit on the hammock   i think so  too  the agreement is untagged  it answers horikita s proposal directly   hammocks  cookware  small tent  lantern  and temporary toilet  fishing rod  a water shower  if we combine those items with the food we purchased  the total comes to exactly seventy points  reads her class s purchases aloud from a manual  seventy points in all   well  let s go over the situation bit by bit  shall we  since there are various places in the woods where we can find fruits and vegetables  we can compensate for deficiencies in points by foraging for food  we can also head out to the sea and fish  that s what i was thinking we d do for food  we re not worried about water  since we have a well  food comes from foraging and the sea  water comes from the well   at first we were worried whether the water was safe to drink    starting this morning  we had everyone use the   well to get water  drinks from the well herself the day before  waits to see if she gets an upset stomach  and only then lets the class use it   also  there s enough natural water that we can use it for showers  that s what a water shower is   after we put water in the tank here  we get hot water in only a few seconds  it s really convenient  we use a gas can for the heat source  when we run out  i plan to request another   no  this is the first i ve heard about or used them  the school s rules are rather scary  aren t they  there weren t any details in the manual  and we can t ask the teacher  either  thankfully we have some kids who are familiar with the outdoors in our class   we set up this temporary toilet instead of getting a shower room  we got it so that the people who dislike being seen by others when they shower could have privacy  the fabric is also waterproof   ah  yeah  at first  i wondered what we were going to do  but then we took appropriate measures  want a look  lifts the tent flap after warning the girls inside and shows the vinyl sheets underfoot   about two centimeters thick   when we paid for the temporary toilet  we were told we had access to an unlimited number of vinyl sheets  so i might have asked for too many  but   we received a large number of them  of course  i don t want to waste resources  so i plan to put any unused vinyl sheets into one sheet  and return them in the end   i wonder if it s because we sprinkle water around  we ve sprinkled water near our beds  because they re close to the well  we put some water in the plastic bottles that people drank from  and then everyone carries them around so they can sprinkle water efficiently  the water soaks into the soil quite easily  and since it takes some time for it to evaporate  the effect lingers and removes the heat  beats the heat with sprinkled water rather than equipment   knowledge  not tools  is what makes the campsite work   i see  having someone retire sounds like it really hurt you guys   i see  well  can we continue our cooperative relationship  i thought it would be a good idea to ignore the rule about trying to find out the leader s identity  what do you think  the cooperation exchange is untagged  the addressee anchors put these lines on her   of course i m okay with that  reaffirms the cooperative relationship with her and agrees to drop the hunt for the leader s identity   yeah  for the time being  anyway  takes the command credit only conditionally   for the time being  knows him from the soccer club and calls him really popular among the girls   ah  from the soccer club  i know him  i know him  he s really popular among the girls   well  if you re okay with something that might be useful  i can tell you something about their place  however  obtaining information is going to be tough   just after you cut through this area  there s an opening  turn right and go straight until you see a cave  that s probably where the class a base camp is  i went there myself to investigate  but i don t know for sure  it s because they re so thoroughly defensive or rather  secretive  has already scouted the class a site herself and marks it as thoroughly defensive   honestly  seeing is believing  if you take a look yourselves  you ll understand right away  since you two are going to check on class a  does that mean you already understand class c s situation  her assessment of class c   no intention of taking the test seriously  five days left  no spot even looked for   runs untagged between her question and the narration that follows  it is left as a chapter attribution gap  takes his interruption patiently  tells him where nakanishi is  and sends him after chihiro chan s group   i think nakanishi kun headed down to the shore  why do you ask   oh no  not at all  i m really happy you feel that way  kaneda kun  can you head over and follow chihiro chan s group  if you tell them i told you to do so  it ll be okay   do you know him  it looks like he had some kind of dispute with class c  he said he d get by on his own  but i couldn t just leave him  i haven t asked him about his situation yet  takes in a class c boy nobody else would take because she couldn t just leave him   and has not yet asked him what happened  hardens when she hears that ibuki was hit   the narration calls it strengthening her resolve to protect her class  closes the visit with farewells after the full exchange of information","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p117-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../people/ichinose-honami.html#sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p117-1\">Ch.3 §3.3: the camp that already works<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.117–125<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../people/ichinose-honami.html\">Ichinose Honami<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Class B&#x27;s base around the well: she is tying a hammock cord to a tree when Horikita and Ayanokōji walk in, and Kanzaki sits a little way off.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../people/horikita-suzune.html\">Horikita Suzune<\/a> · <a href=\"../people/hirata-yousuke.html\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/a> · <a href=\"../people/kaneda-satoru.html\">Kaneda Satoru<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Huh? Horikita-san? And Ayanokouji-kun?”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Ha ha, yeah. It was really difficult at first! But we tried a bunch of different things, and it worked out. Though the list of chores just keeps on increasing. There’s still a ton of work left,”<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ichinose Honami<\/b> “Oh, I’m sorry. That probably sounded like I was trying to drive you guys away. I think it’s all right if you hang around for a while. You probably came here to ask me something, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>41 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> Class B&#x27;s site — trees around a well, hammocks strung for lack of tent space, unfamiliar equipment beside the water.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes the interruption as a welcome rather than an intrusion: smiling, she assumes they came with a question.<span class=\"pg\">p.117<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Welcomes them without any hint of protest and invites them to sit on the hammock.<span class=\"pg\">p.118<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think so, too.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The agreement is untagged; it answers Horikita&#x27;s proposal directly.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hammocks. Cookware. Small tent, lantern, and temporary toilet. Fishing rod, a water shower… If we combine those items with the food we purchased, the total comes to exactly seventy points.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> Reads her class&#x27;s purchases aloud from a manual: seventy points in all.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, let’s go over the situation bit by bit, shall we? Since there are various places in the woods where we can find fruits and vegetables, we can compensate for deficiencies in points by foraging for food. We can also head out to the sea and fish. That’s what I was thinking we’d do for food. We’re not worried about water, since we have a well.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Food comes from foraging and the sea; water comes from the well.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “At first we were worried whether the water was safe to drink, … Starting this morning, we had everyone use the … well to get water.”<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Drinks from the well herself the day before, waits to see if she gets an upset stomach, and only then lets the class use it.<span class=\"pg\">p.120<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Also, there’s enough natural water that we can use it for showers. That’s what a water shower is.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “After we put water in the tank here, we get hot water in only a few seconds. It’s really convenient. We use a gas can for the heat source. When we run out, I plan to request another.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “No. This is the first I’ve heard about or used them. The school’s rules are rather scary, aren’t they? There weren’t any details in the manual, and we can’t ask the teacher, either. Thankfully we have some kids who are familiar with the outdoors in our class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “We set up this temporary toilet instead of getting a shower room. We got it so that the people who dislike being seen by others when they shower could have privacy. The fabric is also waterproof.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah, yeah. At first, I wondered what we were going to do, but then we took appropriate measures. Want a look?”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Lifts the tent flap after warning the girls inside and shows the vinyl sheets underfoot — about two centimeters thick.<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “When we paid for the temporary toilet, we were told we had access to an unlimited number of vinyl sheets. So I might have asked for too many, but … we received a large number of them. Of course, I don’t want to waste resources, so I plan to put any unused vinyl sheets into one sheet, and return them in the end.”<span class=\"pg\">p.121<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I wonder if it’s because we sprinkle water around. We’ve sprinkled water near our beds, because they’re close to the well. We put some water in the plastic bottles that people drank from, and then everyone carries them around so they can sprinkle water efficiently. The water soaks into the soil quite easily, and since it takes some time for it to evaporate, the effect lingers and removes the heat.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Beats the heat with sprinkled water rather than equipment — knowledge, not tools, is what makes the campsite work.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see… Having someone retire sounds like it really hurt you guys.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, can we continue our cooperative relationship? I thought it would be a good idea to ignore the rule about trying to find out the leader’s identity. What do you think?”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The cooperation exchange is untagged; the addressee anchors put these lines on her.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Of course I’m okay with that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Reaffirms the cooperative relationship with her and agrees to drop the hunt for the leader&#x27;s identity.<span class=\"pg\">p.122<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Yeah. For the time being, anyway.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes the command credit only conditionally — for the time being.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Hirata Yōsuke<\/b> Knows him from the soccer club and calls him really popular among the girls.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Ah. From the soccer club! I know him, I know him! He’s really popular among the girls.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well, if you’re okay with something that might be useful, I can tell you something about their place. However, obtaining information is going to be tough.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Just after you cut through this area, there’s an opening. Turn right and go straight until you see a cave. That’s probably where the Class A base camp is. I went there myself to investigate, but I don’t know for sure. It’s because they’re so thoroughly defensive…or rather, secretive.”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Has already scouted the Class A site herself and marks it as thoroughly defensive.<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Honestly, seeing is believing. If you take a look yourselves, you’ll understand right away. Since you two are going to check on Class A, does that mean you already understand Class C’s situation?”<span class=\"pg\">p.123<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her assessment of Class C — no intention of taking the test seriously, five days left, no spot even looked for — runs untagged between her question and the narration that follows; it is left as a chapter attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Kaneda Satoru<\/b> Takes his interruption patiently, tells him where Nakanishi is, and sends him after Chihiro-chan&#x27;s group.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I think Nakanishi-kun headed down to the shore. Why do you ask?”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Oh no, not at all. I’m really happy you feel that way, Kaneda-kun. Can you head over and follow Chihiro-chan’s group? If you tell them I told you to do so, it’ll be okay.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Do you know him? It looks like he had some kind of dispute with Class C. He said he’d get by on his own, but I couldn’t just leave him. I haven’t asked him about his situation yet.”<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Takes in a Class C boy nobody else would take because she couldn&#x27;t just leave him — and has not yet asked him what happened.<span class=\"pg\">p.124<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Hardens when she hears that Ibuki was hit — the narration calls it strengthening her resolve to protect her class.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Horikita Suzune<\/b> Closes the visit with farewells after the full exchange of information.<span class=\"pg\">p.125<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ichinose-honami-y1v3-p149-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: the ghost camp with the Class B pair<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"spoken","w":"totsuka-yahiko ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 3  3 4  the class a cave the cave mouth cut deep into the mountainside like a demon s mouth  with two temporary toilets and a shower room outside  he steps over horikita and walks up to it  the class a site  a cave in the mountainside  its entrance hidden behind vinyl sheets joined into one giant tarp   let s go  i mean  it s class a  so of course we re going to be scared  there s nothing we can do about that   and what do we gain by trying to peek from our hiding spot  we can barely see  and there s no one around  there s not much we can see unless we enter the cave   i haven t thought of anything  come on  don t worry  goes up openly rather than scouting from cover so that he can see inside   and finds the tarp already blocking the view  the opening line on the approach is untagged  horikita s two questions are recorded under her  recognizes yahiko as one of the two who found the cave on the first day  katsuragi is away  the closing judgment   that class a has to be left alone and cannot be investigated   is his  left untagged and recorded here without a quotation","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\">Ch.3 §3.4: the Class A cave<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.126–129<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">The cave mouth cut deep into the mountainside like a demon&#x27;s mouth, with two temporary toilets and a shower room outside; he steps over Horikita and walks up to it.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../people/totsuka-yahiko.html\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Let’s go. I mean, it’s Class A, so of course we’re going to be scared. There’s nothing we can do about that.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “And what do we gain by trying to peek from our hiding spot? We can barely see, and there’s no one around. There’s not much we can see unless we enter the cave.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I haven’t thought of anything. Come on, don’t worry.”<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>5 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The Class A site: a cave in the mountainside, its entrance hidden behind vinyl sheets joined into one giant tarp.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Goes up openly rather than scouting from cover so that he can see inside — and finds the tarp already blocking the view.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The opening line on the approach is untagged; Horikita&#x27;s two questions are recorded under her.<span class=\"pg\">p.126<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Totsuka Yahiko<\/b> Recognizes Yahiko as one of the two who found the cave on the first day; Katsuragi is away.<span class=\"pg\">p.127<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The closing judgment — that Class A has to be left alone and cannot be investigated — is his, left untagged and recorded here without a quotation.<span class=\"pg\">p.129<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p117-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.3: Class B’s camp at the well<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.1: the walk with Sakura<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action inner spoken","w":"sakura-airi ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  4 1  the walk with sakura third day  before noon  he slips out of base camp alone for the forest entrance to see what kouenji had been looking at  and sakura catches up  out of breath  the forest path out of base camp  marked by a handkerchief tied around a tree   didn t i tie a handkerchief around a tree  anyway  i thought i d just go and check something out  the line just above the quoted one prints  didn t had the time  kept as printed   isn t it better for you to stay back  won t it bother you if people start spreading rumors   it s not going to be particularly easy  right  i mean  after we went through all the trouble of coming to this island  i think you should have a little fun  though i m not one to talk about fun  myself  turns her request down with that excuse   she answers that this is fun  crouches and hides her face  and he takes her along after all  accepts her company on one condition  if they get into trouble later  she must not blame herself   well then  how about we go together  but i have a condition  if we get into trouble later  you won t blame yourself  okay   are you getting along well with the other girls  i mean  you can t really do things alone in this test  right   that s not true  you re making progress  sakura chan   it is true  maybe you can t see it  but you re definitely making progress little by little   it s okay  you ll make some friends really soon  sakura  then school will become much more fun  appeals from the bottom of his heart for the first time  choosing words and attitude together  the narration judges it the right method for someone who lacks confidence  her lines carry the narration tags or address him by name  his replies through the walk are untagged and recorded here   that reminds me  that guy  from the incident before it seems like he resigned   i didn t really do anything  you were saved because you got close to kushida  and because horikita and ichinose helped out  i was just a bystander  anyway  more importantly  nothing else weird has happened  right  credits kushida s proximity and horikita and ichinose s help with the stalker affair  his own part was bystander only   besides  even though you usually act nervous  you always had this really confident expression when you were an idol   a long time ago  but when you were featured in magazines you probably didn t take the pictures yourself  right  draws her out on the idol years until she describes erasing herself to endure the shoots  the narration reads her as scarred by the stalker but headed in a better direction   considering even kouenji s satisfaction  the school has probably been really good about keeping up the place  normally  an overseas jungle would be more dangerous  rests with her against one tree half an hour up the steep trail   the longest time alone with her since the landing   and reads the distance between them shortening toward friendship  the first relationship he has felt tilt that way   but if i m in the picture  wouldn t that spoil the scenery  watching her frame the shot with thumb and forefingers   preserving memories  huh  so that was why ibuki had a digital camera  his inference rather than a fact about ibuki  her reason for carrying a camera at school is applied to the class c girl","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1\">Ch.4 §4.1: the walk with Sakura<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.131–135<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Third day, before noon: he slips out of base camp alone for the forest entrance to see what Kouenji had been looking at, and Sakura catches up, out of breath.<\/p><p class=\"with\">with <a href=\"../people/sakura-airi.html\">Sakura Airi<\/a><\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Didn’t I tie a handkerchief around a tree? Anyway, I thought I’d just go and check something out.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Isn’t it better for you to stay back? Won’t it bother you if people start spreading rumors?”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “It’s not going to be particularly easy, right? I mean, after we went through all the trouble of coming to this island, I think you should have a little fun… Though I’m not one to talk about fun, myself.”<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>22 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The forest path out of base camp, marked by a handkerchief tied around a tree.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line just above the quoted one prints “didn’t had the time”; kept as printed.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Turns her request down with that excuse — she answers that this is fun, crouches and hides her face, and he takes her along after all.<span class=\"pg\">p.131<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Accepts her company on one condition: if they get into trouble later, she must not blame herself.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Well then, how about we go together? But I have a condition. If we get into trouble later, you won’t blame yourself. Okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Are you getting along well with the other girls? I mean, you can’t really do things alone in this test, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That’s not true. You’re making progress, Sakura-chan.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It is true. Maybe you can’t see it, but you’re definitely making progress little by little.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “It’s okay. You’ll make some friends really soon, Sakura. Then school will become much more fun.”<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Trait<\/span> Appeals from the bottom of his heart for the first time, choosing words and attitude together; the narration judges it the right method for someone who lacks confidence.<span class=\"pg\">p.132<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> Her lines carry the narration tags or address him by name; his replies through the walk are untagged and recorded here.<span class=\"pg\">p.131–135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “That reminds me… That guy, from the incident before…it seems like he resigned.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I didn’t really do anything. You were saved because you got close to Kushida, and because Horikita and Ichinose helped out. I was just a bystander. Anyway, more importantly, nothing else weird has happened, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Backstory<\/span> Credits Kushida’s proximity and Horikita and Ichinose’s help with the stalker affair; his own part was bystander only.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Besides, even though you usually act nervous, you always had this really confident expression when you were an idol.”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A long time ago? But when you were featured in magazines you probably didn’t take the pictures yourself, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Draws her out on the idol years until she describes erasing herself to endure the shoots; the narration reads her as scarred by the stalker but headed in a better direction.<span class=\"pg\">p.133<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Considering even Kouenji’s satisfaction, the school has probably been really good about keeping up the place. Normally, an overseas jungle would be more dangerous.”<span class=\"pg\">p.134<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Relationship<\/span> <b class=\"sp\">Sakura Airi<\/b> Rests with her against one tree half an hour up the steep trail — the longest time alone with her since the landing — and reads the distance between them shortening toward friendship, the first relationship he has felt tilt that way.<span class=\"pg\">p.134–135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “But if I’m in the picture, wouldn’t that spoil the scenery?”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inner voice<\/span> Watching her frame the shot with thumb and forefingers: “Preserving memories, huh? So that was why Ibuki had a digital camera.”<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> His inference rather than a fact about Ibuki: her reason for carrying a camera at school is applied to the Class C girl.<span class=\"pg\">p.135<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p126-1\">← Before: Ch.3 §3.4: the Class A cave<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 4  4 2  the caterpillar and the corn a hairy caterpillar drops into sakura s hair during the break  pointing it out might make her scream it into her clothes  so he has to remove it without telling her   sakura  there s something i want to ask you   you are you okay with bugs   yeah  bugs  like grasshoppers and dragonflies  those kinds of things   i see  well  all right then   hmm  anyway  don t move for the time being  okay  feigns a casual interest in bugs to learn what she can stand  then holds off acting until he has another way  reaches through his own revulsion   a city boy who hates insects   touches the caterpillar off her hair and throws it into the bushes  she never learns what happened   for the time being  let s investigate the area  but don t go too far  then let s check on each other regularly  if we don t concentrate  it s likely we ll get distracted   did you notice something  about twenty minutes from base camp by the handkerchief marker  the rise where kouenji had stood  finds nothing by sight  then works the soil  the roots  the leaves and the air with all five senses   so  this is what kouenji saw  reads the soil color under the corn and the weed cover around it as artificial cultivation   proof that school officials come and go on the island  the narration answers kouenji s silent gaze from the second day  he saw the corn at first glance and said nothing out of pride   sorry  sorry  i thought it would be okay  wait  what did you mean by  it s too soon   if we tie up the openings of my shirt  we can use it as a bag  that way  we could carry more at once  turns his shirt into a carry bag rather than leave the ears behind for another class to harvest while they are away  the bags line that opens the harvest is untagged   either speaker fits   and is left as an attribution gap","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p137-1\">Ch.4 §4.2: the caterpillar and the corn<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.137–140<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">A hairy caterpillar drops into Sakura’s hair during the break; pointing it out might make her scream it into her clothes, so he has to remove it without telling her.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Sakura, there’s something I want to ask you…”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “You…are you okay with bugs?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Yeah. Bugs. Like grasshoppers and dragonflies, those kinds of things”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>15 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I see. Well, all right then.”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Hmm. Anyway, don’t move for the time being, okay?”<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Feigns a casual interest in bugs to learn what she can stand, then holds off acting until he has another way.<span class=\"pg\">p.137<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reaches through his own revulsion — a city boy who hates insects — touches the caterpillar off her hair and throws it into the bushes; she never learns what happened.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “For the time being, let’s investigate the area, but don’t go too far. Then let’s check on each other regularly. If we don’t concentrate, it’s likely we’ll get distracted.”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Did you notice something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> About twenty minutes from base camp by the handkerchief marker: the rise where Kouenji had stood.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Finds nothing by sight, then works the soil, the roots, the leaves and the air with all five senses.<span class=\"pg\">p.138<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “So, this is what Kouenji saw…”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the soil color under the corn and the weed cover around it as artificial cultivation — proof that school officials come and go on the island.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The narration answers Kouenji’s silent gaze from the second day: he saw the corn at first glance and said nothing out of pride.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, sorry. I thought it would be okay. Wait, what did you mean by ‘it’s too soon’?”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “If we tie up the openings of my shirt, we can use it as a bag. That way… we could carry more at once.”<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Turns his shirt into a carry bag rather than leave the ears behind for another class to harvest while they are away.<span class=\"pg\">p.140<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The bags line that opens the harvest is untagged — either speaker fits — and is left as an attribution gap.<span class=\"pg\">p.139<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p131-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.1: the walk with Sakura<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p140-1\">→ After: Ch.4 §4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/button><\/div><\/article>"},{"i":"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1","v":"y1v3","y":1,"o":3,"k":"action spoken","w":"ayanokouji-kiyotaka","q":"ayanokoji kiyotaka ch 5  the solo sweep toward class a fourth day  laughter has replaced complaint   corn  fish and fruit have the class ahead   when he borrows a ballpoint pen  takes his folded map and walks out of base camp  about 100 points spent in total  koenji s retirement included  at this pace the class ends the test with points left over  and even yukimura has no complaints  breaks the test down 80 20   eighty percent defensive cooperation  twenty percent offensive scouting   with the smaller share deciding outcomes the more  reads the balance as meaning class d now has to attack the other classes  and sets out for class a s area around the cave  the cliff below the cave  a ladder in a blind spot drops to a hut spot with fishing tackle  recalls the facilities seen from the ship  finds the ladder anyone would miss at first glance  and marks the hut s approximate position on his map  the hut spot means fish without borrowing equipment  the device shows class a occupying with four hours remaining  and the dusty tools show the gear itself has not been used  reads the unoccupied tower as deliberate   holding a visible facility risks observation  and katsuragi is too cautious for bait this sweet and this close   so  you won t occupy this spot out of more than a sense of prudence  the line is untagged  it voices his reading of the empty tower a moment before the ambush and is recorded as his  two class a boys spring the trap   one checks the terminal for a fresh claim  one puts a branch to his throat   and the search takes his pen and folded map   i m ayanokouji  from class d   give it back   i can t say   i can t say  if i did i may not be able to return to my class  holds the line through a rapid fire interrogation   three seconds  four seconds of silence   without naming anyone  the offer on the table    there s one more thing i talk to you about  if you tell us the identity of your leader  we re prepared to offer a generous reward  100 000 or 200 000 points    first come  first serve  signed by memorandum and paid after the test   you re asking for me to sell out my class for money   sorry  but i don t believe it  how would you pay someone  we don t   have any cell phones here  right   a memorandum  huh  let me ask you something for my own reference  can you tell me how many points i d get if i did tell you something   could i have someone trustworthy settle things  for example  someone like katsuragi  or perhaps sa  drops katsuragi s name as bait of his own   cut off at  sa  the sentence buys the reaction he was after   i ve heard rumors that katsuragi is class a s representative  their correction    don t make me laugh  sakayanagi is the representative of class a  not katsuragi  you can go now    marks the pair as katsuragi s enemies and puts who really leads class a in question","h":"<article class=\"card\" id=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1\"><h3><span class=\"ttl\"><a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html#sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p144-1\">Ch.5: the solo sweep toward Class A<\/a><\/span><span class=\"meta\">Y1V3 · p.144–148<\/span><span class=\"by\">notes on <a href=\"../people/ayanokouji-kiyotaka.html\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/a><\/span><\/h3><p class=\"setup\">Fourth day: laughter has replaced complaint — corn, fish and fruit have the class ahead — when he borrows a ballpoint pen, takes his folded map and walks out of base camp.<\/p><ul class=\"lines\"><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “So, you won’t occupy this spot out of more than a sense of prudence?”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “I’m Ayanokouji, from Class D.”<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li class=\"q spoken\"><b class=\"sp\">Ayanokōji Kiyotaka<\/b> “Give it back.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><\/ul><details class=\"more\"><summary>20 more notes<\/summary><ul class=\"rows\"><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Numbers<\/span> About 100 points spent in total, Kōenji&#x27;s retirement included; at this pace the class ends the test with points left over, and even Yukimura has no complaints.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Breaks the test down 80:20 — eighty percent defensive cooperation, twenty percent offensive scouting — with the smaller share deciding outcomes the more.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Reads the balance as meaning Class D now has to attack the other classes, and sets out for Class A&#x27;s area around the cave.<span class=\"pg\">p.144<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">The place<\/span> The cliff below the cave: a ladder in a blind spot drops to a hut spot with fishing tackle.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Recalls the facilities seen from the ship, finds the ladder anyone would miss at first glance, and marks the hut&#x27;s approximate position on his map.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The hut spot means fish without borrowing equipment; the device shows Class A occupying with four hours remaining, and the dusty tools show the gear itself has not been used.<span class=\"pg\">p.145<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Reads the unoccupied tower as deliberate — holding a visible facility risks observation, and Katsuragi is too cautious for bait this sweet and this close.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Caveat<\/span> The line is untagged; it voices his reading of the empty tower a moment before the ambush and is recorded as his.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">What happens<\/span> Two Class A boys spring the trap — one checks the terminal for a fresh claim, one puts a branch to his throat — and the search takes his pen and folded map.<span class=\"pg\">p.146<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t say.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I can’t say. If I did…I may not be able to return to my class.”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Feat<\/span> Holds the line through a rapid-fire interrogation — three seconds, four seconds of silence — without naming anyone.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Rule<\/span> The offer on the table — “There’s one more thing I talk to you about. If you tell us the identity of your leader, we’re prepared to offer a generous reward. 100,000 or 200,000 points.” — first-come, first-serve, signed by memorandum and paid after the test.<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “You’re asking for me to sell out my class for money?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Sorry, but I don’t believe it. How would you pay someone? We don’t … have any cell phones here, right?”<span class=\"pg\">p.147<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “A memorandum, huh? Let me ask you something for my own reference… Can you tell me how many points I’d get if I did tell you something?”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “Could I have someone trustworthy settle things? For example, someone like Katsuragi. Or perhaps Sa—”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Tactic<\/span> Drops Katsuragi&#x27;s name as bait of his own — cut off at “Sa—”, the sentence buys the reaction he was after.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Spoken<\/span> “I’ve heard rumors that Katsuragi is Class A’s representative.”<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><li><span class=\"mlabel\">Inference, not stated<\/span> Their correction — “Don’t make me laugh. Sakayanagi is the representative of Class A. Not Katsuragi. You can go now.” — marks the pair as Katsuragi&#x27;s enemies and puts who really leads Class A in question.<span class=\"pg\">p.148<\/span><\/li><\/ul><\/details><div class=\"ptrs\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p140-1\">← Before: Ch.4 §4.3: Katsuragi at the cornfield<\/button><button type=\"button\" class=\"ptr\" data-go=\"sc-ayanokouji-kiyotaka-y1v3-p149-1\">→ After: Ch.5 §5.1: the ghost camp and the Class A question<\/button><\/div><\/article>"}];
